  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 220 AM EDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nBroad midlevel ridging extending across the Gulf Coast states \nmidweek will begin flattening as a trough digs into the Great \nLakes region. By Thursday, the core of the ridge will have shifted\nwell westward into the southwestern US with troughing digging \nfarther southeastward by the week's end.\n\nMeanwhile, at the surface, easterly flow associated with an \nearly- week CAD setup will transition to the southwest by Thursday\nin response to the surface high departing eastward and a cold \nfront dropping into the Ohio Valley. As such, PoPs look to \nincrease most appreciably by Thursday into Friday as moisture is \npulled back northward in advance of the approaching cold front. \nThis frontal boundary will provide impetus for increased \nconvective coverage heading into next weekend.\n\nAs far as temperatures are concerned, the initial early week \n\"cooldown\" to more normal levels for September will revert back to\na warming trend through late week. Above-normal highs in the 90s \nmake a return with heat index values likely creeping back into the\nupper 90s to near 100 for many.",
